  "acceptance": "Close the measure-growth half of U9 at the scalar/model level. Consume the round-3 files release/Poincare/L4/Compactness/DoublingToCovers.lean and release/Poincare/L4/Compactness/MeasureGrowthCovers.lean together with D12's Poincare/D12/ComparisonGeodesics/VolumeRatio.lean (bishopGromov_volume_le, bishopGromovVolumeRatio) and Poincare/D12/ComparisonGeodesics/ModelEuclidean.lean (euclidModelA, euclidModelM, euclidModel_volume). Required content: (1) instantiate bishopGromov_volume_le with an EXPLICIT comparison model (Euclidean euclidModelA d / euclidModelM d for k >= 0; the constant-curvature hyperbolic model for k <= K <= 0 if available) and prove the volume-ratio bound in closed form radialVolume A R <= (R/r)^(d+1) * radialVolume A r (respectively the hyperbolic closed form); (2) derive the single-scale doubling consequence radialVolume A (2r) <= 2^(d+1) * radialVolume A r with a non-vacuous witness; (3) state PRECISELY, as a documented interface (not an assumed theorem), which additional hypothesis would realize radialVolume A as a genuine ball measure mu (mu (closedBall x s) = radialVolume A s) and hence discharge the hupper/hlower hypotheses of Poincare.L4.Compactness.coveringNumber_le_measure_ratio and coveringNumber_le_of_measure_doubling; do NOT claim that a manifold measure exists; (4) every declaration must list its analytic hypotheses explicitly and be labelled model (scalar ODE) versus manifold. Acceptance evidence: compiling modules with full signatures, source hashes, compile exits, fail-closed axiom audit with cones subset {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, non-vacuous witnesses, and an adversarial semantic review confirming no conclusion-equivalent hypothesis and no manifold overclaim. Do not assume Bishop-Gromov as a hypothesis and do not duplicate the existing conjugate_point_bound/Rauch results.",
